//! The Saw file a C image still has to have.
//!
//! The image this package builds is C (`crt0.c`, `syscall.c`, `main.c`) and
//! carries no Saw. But `emit = "sosimg"` is Blade's target, and Blade's
//! `build_sos_image` opens with `find_source_file()`, which looks for
//! `src/main.saw`, then `main.saw`, then `src/lib.saw` and refuses the build
//! with "No main.saw or lib.saw found" when there is none. A package of pure C
//! is not expressible; a package of pure C plus this file is.
//!
//! The object `sawc --freestanding` produces from this file has an empty
//! `.text` and defines no symbol anything references. It still carries the
//! static backtrace table, `.rodata.__saw_bt_table`, which is marked RETAIN,
//! so `--gc-sections` keeps it. That is a constant per image, not per Saw
//! declaration.
//!
//! The entry is the C crt0 (`ENTRY(_start)`), the one loadable segment is
//! clang's code and `.rodata`, and `_arena_start` and `_arena_end` coincide
//! because the package's linker script sets `ARENA_SIZE` to 0.
//!
//! Nothing below this line: a declaration here would be a declaration in the
//! image.
